## Why This Is Asked
Tests integration of REST, WebSocket, and Service Worker in a practical frontend scenario with offline considerations and real DOM updates. It probes data freshness, reconnection strategies, and efficient rendering under network variability.

## Key Concepts
- DOM diffing: efficient patching to update only changed rows
- REST + caching: per-URL TTL, lastUpdate, and offline fallback
- WebSocket: robust reconnect with exponential backoff
- Service Worker: offline caching for assets and latest payload
- Reconciliation: merge in-flight WS updates after reconnect without data loss

## Code Example
```javascript
// Lightweight patch helper (conceptual)
function patchRows(container, changes) {
  changes.forEach(({ id, data }) => {
    const row = container.querySelector(`[data-id="${id}"]`);
    if (row) {
      Object.assign(row.dataset, data);
      row.textContent = data.status;
    } else {
      const el = document.createElement('div');
      el.dataset.id = id;
      el.textContent = data.status;
      container.appendChild(el);
    }
  });
}
```

